<title>USA: JPE closes buy of Canadian auto trim firm.</title>
<headline>JPE closes buy of Canadian auto trim firm.</headline>
<dateline>ANN ARBOR, Mich. 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>JPE Inc said Monday it completed its acquisition of Pebra Inc, a manufacturer of auto trim parts, for about $23.2 million.</p>
<p>JPE said the new company, known as JPE Canada, will continue to make plastic injection-molded fascias, rocker panels and body-side moldings for the automotive industry. JPE Canada is expected to post annual sales of $60 million, the new parent firm said.</p>
<p>JPE acquires and develops companies that make or distribute automobile and truck components.</p>
<p>Its stock closed unchanged Monday at 7-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
